<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
	<Task>
		<Title>OS Config: Rename Domain Computer (PowerShell one-liner)</Title>
		<Description><![CDATA[<P><STRONG><FONT size=3>About this Task</FONT></STRONG></P>
<BLOCKQUOTE style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px" dir=ltr>
<P>This task renames the local computer and unjoins it from the Domain.</P>
<P>This task is applicable on:&nbsp;Windows&nbsp;with version 9.0+ of the BESClient.</P>
<P>This implementation passes PowerShell script via an 'echo' command.&nbsp; This eliminates needing to save the credentials to a file on-disk, with the cost of added complexity on character escaping.</P></BLOCKQUOTE>
<P dir=ltr><LABEL for=secret><STRONG><FONT size=3>Action Description</FONT></STRONG></LABEL></P>
<UL dir=ltr>
<LI>
<DIV style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px"><LABEL for=secret><STRONG>Action1: Rename the computer.</STRONG></LABEL></DIV></LI></UL>
<BLOCKQUOTE style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px" dir=ltr>
<P style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px"><LABEL for=secret>This action prompts for an existing&nbsp;local user account name and changes&nbsp;its password to the value specified in the "Password" field under "Customization Options".</LABEL></P>
<P style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px"><LABEL for=secret></LABEL><LABEL for=secret><STRONG><FONT color=#008000 size=3>Customization Options</FONT></STRONG></LABEL></P></BLOCKQUOTE>
<BLOCKQUOTE style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px" dir=ltr>
<P>
<TABLE>
<TBODY>
<TR>
<TD><LABEL for=secret>Current Domain Name:</LABEL> </TD>
<TD><INPUT id=domainname name=domainname></TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD><LABEL for=secret>Domain Account:</LABEL> </TD>
<TD><INPUT id=userd name=userd></TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD><LABEL for=secret>Domain Account Password:</LABEL> </TD>
<TD><INPUT id=passwordd type=password name=passwordd> </TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD><LABEL for=secret>New Computername:</LABEL> </TD>
<TD><INPUT id=newname name=newname> </TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE><script>
                                                   document.body.ontakeaction = function() {
                                                                    var params = [ document.getElementById( "domainname" ).value,
																		document.getElementById( "userd" ).value,
																		document.getElementById( "passwordd" ).value,
																		document.getElementById( "newname" ).value
																		];
																	var valid=true;
																	for (i=0, len = params.length; i < len; i++) {
																		if (params[i] == null || params[i]=="") 
																		{
																		 valid=false;
																		}																	
																																															;
																	}
																		
																	if (valid==false)
																		{alert("Hey, you forgot to enter a secure parameter! Please fill out the Description tab before taking the action.");}																	
                                                                    else
																		{TakeSecureFixletAction( Relevance('id of current fixlet'), Relevance('id of current bes site'), "Action1", {}, { 
																			domainname: document.getElementById( "domainname" ).value, userd: document.getElementById( "userd" ).value, passwordd: document.getElementById( "passwordd" ).value, newname: document.getElementById( "newname" ).value	} );
																		}
                                                                    return false;
                                                   }
                                                   </script> </P></BLOCKQUOTE>
<P dir=ltr><STRONG><FONT color=#ff0000 size=3>Important Notes</FONT></STRONG></P>
<UL dir=ltr>
<LI>
<DIV>You must enter a Domain credential and password in order to take an action</DIV>
<LI>Because of the way secure parameters work, you cannot use this task in&nbsp;a baseline, target an action dynamically by property (e.g., automatic groups), use add additional actions.</LI></UL>]]></Description>
		<Relevance>windows of operating system</Relevance>
		<Relevance>if exists property "in proxy agent context" then not in proxy agent context else true</Relevance>
		<Relevance><![CDATA[version of client >= "9.0"]]></Relevance>
		<Category>OS Configuration</Category>
		<DownloadSize>0</DownloadSize>
		<Source>Internal</Source>
		<SourceID></SourceID>
		<SourceReleaseDate>2026-09-02</SourceReleaseDate>
		<SourceSeverity></SourceSeverity>
		<CVENames></CVENames>
		<SANSID></SANSID>
		<MIMEField>
			<Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
			<Value>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 16:27:59 +0000</Value>
		</MIMEField>
		<Domain>BESC</Domain>
		<DefaultAction ID="Action1">
			<Description>
				<PreLink></PreLink>
				<Link>Rename</Link>
				<PostLink><![CDATA[&nbsp;the computer]]></PostLink>
			</Description>
			<ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell"><![CDATA[action log all

action uses wow64 redirection false

waithidden cmd.exe /c "echo  Write-Output 'Rename-Computer' ; try {{ $password = ConvertTo-SecureString '{parameter "passwordd" of action}' -AsPlainText -Force ; $cred = New-Object System.Management.Automation.PSCredential ^('{parameter "domainname" of action}\{parameter "userd" of action}', $password^) ; Rename-Computer -NewName '{parameter "newname" of action}' -DomainCredential $cred -Restart -Force -ErrorAction Stop ; Write-Output 'Rename-Computer Succeeded' ; exit 0 } catch {{  [Console]::Error.WriteLine('Rename-Computer Failed: ' + $_.Exception.Message) ; exit 1 } | powershell.exe -NoProfile -Command -   > \RenameDomainComputer.out 2>&1
continue if {exit code of action = 0 }
action requires restart "RenameDomainComputer"]]></ActionScript>
			<SuccessCriteria Option="RunToCompletion"></SuccessCriteria>
		</DefaultAction>
	</Task>
</BES>
